{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Managing the Restaurant"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Dealing with Difficult Customers"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.  "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.  "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le05ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional: Possibility, Warnings and Threats"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the First Conditional with If clauses to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will or will not happen. The outcome is not in the present, but in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">If you focus more on our customers, they'll leave a larger tip.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You also use the First Conditional to suggest a warning or a threat."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">If you don't focus on our customers, we'll keep on getting bad reviews.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple \u2026 will + verb \u2026</spa"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you get your customer to calm down, listen, and address the situation, you will need to deal with their emotional state. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you don't reduce the customer's emotional level, they will not listen to you or be receptive to what you are saying or your attempts to assist. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If your customer perceives that you are not attuned to their emotional needs or thinks that you are not working in their best interest, you will become part of the problem, rather than part of the solution."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Willingness, Refusal, Promises and Threats "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\"> won't</span> to express willingness, refusal, promise and threat in situations in the present or in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are different ways to use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">won't</span>. In the following uses, we don't necessarily talk about a future action or an event that will take place at a point in time in the future. Instead, <span class=\"italic\">will</span> or <span class=\"italic\">won't</span> are used to express willingness, refusal, promise or threat related to an action which could be in the present or in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the following examples:<ul><li>Willingness:</li> <span class=\"italic\">Will you clean the restaurant kitchen with me, please?</span> <li>Refusal:</li> <span class=\"italic\">I will not tolerate this behavior in the kitchen any longer.</span><br/><span class=\"italic\">The computer won't start.</span><li>Promise:</li> <span class=\"italic\">I'll do everything I can to satisfy our customers.</span> <li>Threat:</li> <span class=\"italic\">If you refuse to help me, I'll have to take extreme measures.</span></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I don't speak to the manager soon, I will never come back here again!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will not be spoken to like that by your employees."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will do everything in my power to help you."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Would you like to speak to the manager now?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Will you be able to come in tomorrow?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "emotional state "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the condition relating to your feelings "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will need to deal with their emotional state. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when dealing with a customer."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "willingness "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the state of being prepared to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to demonstrate the willingness to listen calmly to what the customer has to say. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to interject "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to interrupt what someone else is saying with a sudden remark "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Listen calmly to what they have to say without interjecting your views. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "attuned to "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "able to \u200bunderstand"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If your customer perceives that you are not attuned to their emotional need, you will become part of the problem."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to acknowledge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "recognized as noticed or heard "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Keep in mind that a customer generally wants to be respected and acknowledged as an individual and as being important. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "interaction"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the activity of talking to other people "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Take one more opportunity at the end of your interaction to send a customer-focused message."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Work with a classmate to create a role play between a salesperson and an angry customer. (You can be a salesperson at any store. Use your imagination!)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of reasons why a customer might be angry."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of what a salesperson might do to alleviate this situation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a dialogue and write it down or take notes so you don't forget what you want to say. Remember to make it sound as natural as possible."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practise the dialogue with your classmate."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Act out the dialogue for your class. Use appropriate body language."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss which dialogue sounded the most natural or the most polite."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write down what I want to say."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use expressions to soften the situation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practise the dialogue out aloud with my classmate."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use body language to help express myself in the role play."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give feedback on the dialogues and discuss how they sounded."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about work and dealing with customers. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express that a fairly certain condition will be fulfilled using <span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">when </span> </span>or <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">if</span></span>"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express willingness and refusal, and make promises and threats."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Have you ever been a difficult customer? Why? What happened? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think it is important to stay calm and listen when a customer is upset? Why or why not?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "How do we deal with a difficult customer? "}], "questions": [], "id": 0}, {"type": "STI", "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Vanessa talks about dealing with a difficult customer, and how <span class=